  },
  "content": {
    "component": "news_article",
    "_uid": "2174-root",
    "title": "A first of many: Somalia's first female pathologist",
    "subtitle": null,
    "summary": "Dr Sagal Salad graduated with a Master of Medicine degree in anatomical pathology from AKU",
    "media": [
      {
        "_uid": "e5c1492492f65d45",
        "component": "news_media",
        "role": "banner",
        "filename": "2174-BannerImage.JPG",
        "src": "/news-media/2174-BannerImage.JPG",
        "media_type": "image",
        "caption": "Dr Sagal Salad graduated with a Master of Medicine degree in anatomical pathology from AKU",
        "alt": "A first of many: Somalia's first female pathologist"
      }
    ],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Dr Sagal Salad carries herself with grace and humility. Do not be fooled by her demeanour, she carries a huge crown - Somalia's first female pathologist. Dr Salad graduated with a Master of Medicine degree in anatomical pathology from AKU. We caught up with her at the February convocation in Nairobi to know more about her story. "
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n      "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Why did you decide to pursue medicine as a career?",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "I developed an interest in health issues when I was in middle school and the interest grew until I completed high school. I then pursued an undergraduate degree in medicine and surgery at a Chinese University. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n      "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Why did you decide to join AKU to pursue your postgraduate degree? ",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "I wanted hands-on clinical experience and mentorship that was relevant to the African context. I was introduced to AKU by a Somali surgical consultant who was working in Nairobi. He told me that I would get everything I needed to advance my career and specialty in pathology at the Aga Khan University. I applied and was pleased to be among the few who got selected. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n      "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "And in pathology because...",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We don't have many pathologists in Africa and in the world. Many doctors prefer other departments because of the face-to-face interaction with the patient. In pathology, you're behind-the-scenes, you don't get to meet the patient. However, I feel it is the core of medicine because without proper diagnosis you're unable to treat a patient. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n      "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "How was the AKU programme? ",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The residency programme is tough (laughs) but it is worth it. The mentorship, practical experience and colleagues are all top notch. I really enjoyed my time at AKU and will miss my friends, faculty and staff at the Aga Khan University Hospital, Nairobi. One of my highlights was a research presentation I made at the 2019 Early-Career Health Researchers' Conference. I was not only exposed to research from other medical fields but received valuable insight from the keynote speakers. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n      "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Why did you decide to go back home? ",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "I wanted to return to Somalia because the population is high and the pathologists are few. I want to use my knowledge and skills to serve my community and country. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "\n      "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Now that you've graduated, what next? ",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "For now, I want to practice pathology - to give proper and accurate diagnosis to patients. My long term goals include running free medical clinics for tumor patients to get proper diagnosis and treatment. I also want to open a free clinic for cancer patients.  "
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
